The transformed turbulence fixture uses linearRGB. A fixed-seed noise control
agrees with the sampled Donner output, and the released image keeps the default
comparison. The explicit sRGB control eliminates the measured Donner/resvg
difference. The archived image also differs in alpha, which is independent of
the color transfer.

The four marker fixtures draw the same five clipped squares and produce the same
resvg image. The top clip edge covers exactly half of the pixel at (230, 12).
The resvg reference has alpha 127 there, and equivalent rectangles give 128
in Firefox and Chrome. The Chrome marker and Donner Metal captures give 0 and
255 respectively. The default comparator excludes antialiased edges. Its passing
result permits this difference in the underlying clip coverage.

