half-alpha crossing on the scanline y=100 lies at x=54.0 in upstream's reference, as in Chrome and
Firefox; the snapshot's crosses at x=53.33. Donner draws image-rendering="optimizeSpeed" with
nearest-neighbor sampling, and upstream's on-feImage reference samples the embedded 64x64 image
at destination pixel centers: every pixel of the 216x216 filter region is within one level of the
texel nearest its center, where the snapshot's samples a different grid. Filter functions operate
in sRGB (Filter Effects 1, section 5), so grayscale() of seagreen gives 115, the interior of
upstream's url-and-grayscale reference; the snapshot's interior is 122, the result for linearRGB
values. Donner matches upstream's three references at default parameters on both CPU text tiers
